```c
} else if (pval > valbuf + JSON_VAL_MAX - 1 || pval > valbuf + maxlen - 1) {
    return JSON_ERR_STRLONG;
}
```

This is checked AFTER `*cp == '"'`. So if `pval` is at `valbuf + maxlen` (one past max), and we see `"`, it writes `*pval++ = '\0'` at `valbuf + maxlen`. This is a WRITE. For `t_string`, `maxlen = len - 1 = 127`. So writing at `valbuf + 127` is within `valbuf` (513 bytes). Fine.

